{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649260",
      "title": "Outputting List Data Dynamically",
      "sourceHash": "f522c23cc9b11a38517b484e7ea1c47ac2954a6153b6dbc635d27383002e22d8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.42,
          "end": 1.92,
          "en": "Now at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.92,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "this first demo application is pretty much finished.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "It has all the features we want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "but there's still something that can be improved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 17.79,
          "en": "And specifically it's this area which can be improved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.79,
          "end": 21.603,
          "en": "Though I don't mean the visuals, but the underlying code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "Because in here in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 28.74,
          "en": "we got these four core concept items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.74,
          "end": 30.333,
          "en": "being displayed like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "Now the problem with this approach here is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "we manually repeat this core concept component four times",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 44.76,
          "en": "in our code because I have four data entries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.76,
          "end": 46.983,
          "en": "in this core concepts array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "But if I were to remove one of these entries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 54.18,
          "en": "by commenting it out, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.18,
          "end": 56.37,
          "en": "the app would therefore kind of break",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.37,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "and we would see this broken element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 63.63,
          "en": "because I still try to output four elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.63,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "So besides us repeating this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "and therefore doing some unnecessary typing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "this approach also has the disadvantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 77.09,
          "en": "of potentially breaking if the data source gets changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.1,
          "end": 80.4,
          "en": "So if for example, one element gets removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "and therefore it would be better if the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "of core concept Components here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "would be derived dynamically based on the number of items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 92.64,
          "en": "we have in this core concepts array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.64,
          "end": 95.82,
          "en": "So if you could simply output one core concept component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.82,
          "end": 98.88300000000001,
          "en": "per entry in that array automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "And that is thankfully something we can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "Now to understand how we can output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "this list here dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 110.43,
          "en": "it's first of all important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.43,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "that you can output an array of data in JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.57,
          "en": "You can output it dynamically, and that could be an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 121.593,
          "en": "of strings like Hello and World.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 125.74,
          "en": "If I would save this, you would see this text here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.41,
          "end": 132.41,
          "en": "but it can also be an array of JSX elements like hello",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 136.773,
          "en": "in a paragraph and World in a paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 140.823,
          "en": "And therefore now you would see this output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 146.84,
          "en": "So JSX is capable of dealing with arrays of renderable data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.143,
          "en": "arrays of JSX code, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 157.56,
          "en": "Now here we have an array of JavaScript objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "and JSX is not really able to output that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 162.3,
          "en": "and it especially, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.3,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "does not know that this image data should be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 167.733,
          "en": "in a image element and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 168.78,
          "end": 172.56,
          "en": "But since JSX is capable of outputting an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 172.56,
          "end": 174.84,
          "en": "of JSX elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.84,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "we could try to transform this array of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 181.113,
          "en": "to an array of JSX elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 182.19,
          "end": 183.93,
          "en": "So here in this unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.93,
          "end": 186.75,
          "en": "we can output something dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.75,
          "end": 191.13,
          "en": "and the something I wanna output is my core concepts array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.13,
          "end": 194.71,
          "en": "transformed to an array of JSX elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "and you can transform arrays in JavaScript with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 202.233,
          "en": "of the built-in map method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 203.4,
          "end": 207.75,
          "en": "Which produces a new array based on the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.75,
          "end": 211.59,
          "en": "For that map takes a JavaScript function, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 211.59,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "such an arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 217.62,
          "en": "And that function will automatically receive an array item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 217.62,
          "end": 218.733,
          "en": "as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 219.78,
          "end": 222.54,
          "en": "And here I'll name it concept item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.54,
          "end": 224.073,
          "en": "though that name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 225.24,
          "end": 230.24,
          "en": "Because this function will now be executed by JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "for every item in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 236.63,
          "en": "So at the moment, three times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 236.63,
          "end": 238.68,
          "en": "since I have three elements in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 238.68,
          "end": 241.353,
          "en": "since the last element is currently commented out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 242.37,
          "end": 244.02,
          "en": "And we will get that item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 244.02,
          "end": 247.263,
          "en": "for every execution as a value for this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.55,
          "end": 252.06,
          "en": "So inside of this arrow function, we can then return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 252.06,
          "end": 256.23,
          "en": "the code we want to transform this item too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 256.23,
          "end": 258.39,
          "en": "So in this case, we wanna transform it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258.39,
          "end": 262.14300000000003,
          "en": "to this core concept component being used as JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.34,
          "end": 265.65,
          "en": "But of course now we no longer access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.65,
          "end": 269.22,
          "en": "a specific core concept index here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 269.22,
          "end": 272.01,
          "en": "Instead, we use this concept item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 272.01,
          "end": 274.71,
          "en": "because that already is one of those items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.71,
          "end": 276.363,
          "en": "in this core concepts array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 282.51,
          "en": "So what we previously manually accessed by index here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.51,
          "end": 286.68,
          "en": "step by step, can now be accessed automatically with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 286.68,
          "end": 287.883,
          "en": "of this map method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 288.75,
          "end": 291.33,
          "en": "Item by item, since as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 291.33,
          "end": 295.74,
          "en": "this function executes once for every item in the array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 295.74,
          "end": 298.29,
          "en": "and therefore this is a quick and easy way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 298.29,
          "end": 300.99,
          "en": "of dynamically generating this list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 300.99,
          "end": 304.09,
          "en": "and therefore now we can get rid of all this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 305.1,
          "end": 309.693,
          "en": "and just use this map method to output a list of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 310.56,
          "end": 314.94,
          "en": "And that's another super useful feature and pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 314.94,
          "end": 317.79,
          "en": "because as it turns out, and as you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 317.79,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "throughout this course, in React apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 324.153,
          "en": "you will often output lists of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 324.99,
          "end": 329.1,
          "en": "And you will almost always do that by using the map method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 329.1,
          "end": 332.433,
          "en": "to transform your data to JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 334.14,
          "end": 336.03,
          "en": "And therefore, now if you saved it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 336.03,
          "end": 341.03,
          "en": "we now have these three items here generated dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 341.25,
          "end": 343.54,
          "en": "and if I go back to data JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 344.374,
          "end": 346.413,
          "en": "and I comment this last item back in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 347.67,
          "end": 350.403,
          "en": "you see that now we have four items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 351.6,
          "end": 354.24,
          "en": "Without us changing the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 354.24,
          "end": 357.633,
          "en": "because that list is now generated dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 359.19,
          "end": 361.89,
          "en": "What you'll also see is that if you open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 361.89,
          "end": 365.223,
          "en": "the developer tools, you get a warning there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 366.39,
          "end": 369.66,
          "en": "A warning that each child in a list should have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 369.66,
          "end": 374.43,
          "en": "a unique key prop and I'll get back to that later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 374.43,
          "end": 377.73,
          "en": "in the course because it's a bit more advanced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 377.73,
          "end": 381.45,
          "en": "But in the end, what you must do to get rid of that warning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 381.45,
          "end": 384.843,
          "en": "is you must add a key prop to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 385.98,
          "end": 388.47,
          "en": "Even though we're not using this prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 388.47,
          "end": 390.6,
          "en": "inside of the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 390.6,
          "end": 394.08,
          "en": "Here, I'm not trying to use a key prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 394.08,
          "end": 397.83299999999997,
          "en": "but still we must add it because it will be used by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 398.74,
          "end": 401.64,
          "en": "It's a special prop, understood and used by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 401.64,
          "end": 405.93,
          "en": "and this key prop can therefore be added to any component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 405.93,
          "end": 408.24,
          "en": "It can be added to built-in elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 408.24,
          "end": 411.153,
          "en": "and to custom Components as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 412.17,
          "end": 415.05,
          "en": "And this value for this key prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 415.05,
          "end": 420.05,
          "en": "should be a value that uniquely identifies a list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 421.14,
          "end": 425.16,
          "en": "Under the hood, it's used by React to efficiently render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 425.16,
          "end": 427.44,
          "en": "and update this list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 427.44,
          "end": 432.04,
          "en": "So here we could use the title as a unique value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 433.05,
          "end": 436.02,
          "en": "because every item here has a different title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 436.02,
          "end": 439.02,
          "en": "So that will be a unique value and it is a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 439.02,
          "end": 442.56,
          "en": "that can be used to tell these different items apart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 442.56,
          "end": 445.353,
          "en": "and that's exactly what this key prop is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 446.34,
          "end": 449.94,
          "en": "So with that special prop added here, the list still looks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 449.94,
          "end": 453.213,
          "en": "as it did before, but now the warning is gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 454.44,
          "end": 455.88,
          "en": "And that's there for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 455.88,
          "end": 458.913,
          "en": "how you can output list content dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}